From 6c0eca49244d901d2f1dc6fc0bbd43bfe9bf33a9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shammah Chancellor <shammah.chancellor@notvalid.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 17:34:39 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] metrics: sealed headers, Merklix, snapshots, fast sync,
 templates, capacity

This tier's own mechanisms - sealed-header block rebuilds, Merklix set
reconciliation, lock-free chain/mempool snapshots, UTXO snapshot (fast)
sync, block templates and the adaptive block capacity - kept their
figures in internal stats structs, debug logs or RPCs, if anywhere.

- fullnode_sealed_headers_total{outcome=rebuilt|already_have|fallback|
  invalid|rejected}, counted beside V2ProtocolHandlerStats' own counters
  in HandleSealedHeader (overlay rebuild succeeded, data already here,
  compact-block fallback requested, malformed, header/coinbase refused).
- fullnode_merklix_rounds_total{round=summary|bucket,
  result=matched|differences}, fullnode_merklix_difference_size{round}
  (short ids found missing in rounds that decoded some) and
  fullnode_merklix_overflows_total (sub-buckets beyond their sketch's
  capacity), in HandleMerklixSync and HandleMerklixBuck.
- fullnode_snapshot_publications_total{kind=chain_tip|best_header|
  mempool} and fullnode_snapshot_publish_seconds{kind}: each publication
  that is built (deferred or skipped ones are not), timed from after the
  deferral checks to the atomic store.
- fullnode_snapshot_sync_state{state} (one-hot over the six swarm
  states), _pivot_height, _shards{status=total|verified|pending|
  in_flight}, _coins_imported, _blocks_peeled, _peers{status=active|
  banned}: GetFastSyncSwarmStatus at scrape time (the handler's mutex,
  briefly, as getfastsyncinfo takes it).
- fullnode_block_template_build_seconds{stage=select|validity|total}:
  CreateNewBlock's existing bench timers.
- fullnode_adaptive_block_size_bytes{limit=max|target|max_generated|ema}
  and fullnode_adaptive_block_size_history_complete: the fee hysteresis
  controller's getters at scrape time (its own mutex).

Transaction-relay announcement metrics are deliberately not added here:
the Nucleation relay lane adds them under this naming scheme.

Cardinality: sealed headers 5, merklix rounds 4, difference size 2,
overflows 1, snapshot publications 3, publish seconds 3, sync state 6,
pivot 1, shards 4, coins 1, peeled 1, peers 2, template seconds 3,
adaptive 4 + 1.

Hot paths: PublishMempoolSnapshot runs on every mempool change; with
-metrics it adds two clock reads, a counter add and a ring push to work
that clones the snapshot. Sealed header and Merklix handlers add a
counter add or ring push per message. No lock is added. Measured with
the benches at the end of the series.

Tests: test/util/metrics.h's ScopedNodeMetrics turns the node's metrics
on in a unit test (leaving the object allocated, as the node does).

Evidence:
- v2_protocol_handler_tests pass, with new checks: the sealed header test
  counts one fallback and one rebuild (matching the handler's stats);
  the Merklix test counts one summary and one bucket round with
  differences per scope (4 each), difference sizes summing to 4 and 8,
  no overflow.
- interface_metrics_tier.py: label sets present; fast sync idle with no
  shards; adaptive limits positive; mining four blocks builds four
  templates (each stage timed) and publishes chain-tip and mempool
  snapshots, each timed; the second node, with high-bandwidth shorttx on,
  rebuilds blocks from sealed headers.

Not tested: Merklix in a functional test (the node only answers peers'
reconciliation, it does not start it); a fast sync session; overflows;
best-header publications.

Coordinator integration provenance (reference405):
Preserve earlier purposeful source repairs through downstream consumer/context adaptations; exact conflict ledger retained.
All60 authored input payloads retained, with prerequisite-aware same-purpose splits; distinct legacy-index and inherited CXX compatibility remain independent. Pre-format source equals exact403+all60 control tree95718fceff83364b74294a751bd752b2f1a4e384. Only pinnedRuff import/format cleanup follows. Original author commands/hashes are historical reference evidence, not combined405 approval. Reference OFF/native/Rust full gates are preserved separately; combined compile/runtime NOT_RUN.
